re like  classic Sims FreePlay the biggest  difference between the PC and console  versions was that there was an object  limiter on the console version limiting  the number of items a player could place  in their houses some items in buy mode  had to be unlocked in the getalife  campaign and houses could only have one  floor it also featured a rudimentary  multiplayer mode bustin out the next  console release was a very similar game  with a single-player story and a free  play mode but this time your sim could  get out of the house and visit other  locations the irbs sims in the city  offered some tweaks to the usual sims  formula as well as building  relationships and fulfilling needs your  sim which for some reason was now called  an herb had to build rep with other  herbs to gain fame and fortune and  advance to new districts in herbs ville  the herbs was the first Sims game to  feature a weather system and its music  was written and performed in Simlish by  the Black Eyed Peas  it was a very different time  [Music]  like its predecessor Sims two players  could build and furnish homes customized  Sims with the extensive character  creation tools and guide them through  their everyday lives but unlike the  first game The Sims themselves were now  a lot more complicated in the sims 1  they just required their basic needs to  be met but now they had personality they  would form memories and had distinct  once and fears which would feed into an  ultimate life goal sims could now be  family or career oriented or they could  long for money or power adjusting your  sims daily routine to meet once and  avoid fears added new challenging layers  to the gameplay if you wanted the best  of your sims you had to work for it  but the biggest change was the addition  of genetics in The Sims 1 there was no  guarantee that a child would resemble  either of its parents into after a  successful woohoo the female sim could  fall pregnant and the resulting baby  would inherit not only its appearance  but aspects of its personality from both  its parents babies could now grow up and  eventually have children of their own  Sims passed through six life stages with  each offering unique age related  experiences toddlers could be taught to  walk and talk children had to go to  school teenagers could have their first  kiss adults could marry and have their  own children and elders would eventually  die sims would remember important life  events both positive and negative and if  they constantly met their goals they'd  live happier longer lives  coupled with the family tree tool  families could now be complex with  lineage full of memories and stories  that you could revisit at a glance it  allowed players to become even more  invested in their Sims lives than ever  before but it wasn't just the Sims that  received some huge fan requested changes  players could now view the world in full  3d thanks to the game's new engine days  of the week were added build and buy  mode received their share of gameplay  tweaks and new objects and create a sim  was radically overhauled to improve  civic customization instead of choosing  from pre-made sim heads and clothes it  now allowed you to customize  almost every aspect of your Sims from  their face and body shaped the color of  their eyes a tool called the body shop  came packaged with the game and allowed  players to create custom clothing and  import it straight in to create a sim  Sims could now have a different outfit  for different occasions and personality  points and aspirations could be assigned  the Sims 2 was a hit with both critics  and the players and sold a million  copies in just 10 days  and hitting 4.5 million by the end of  its first year but the game wasn't  without its controversies former Florida  Attorney Jack Thompson called for the  game to be banned claiming that EA were  promoting nudity because certain mods  and cheat codes could remove the Sims  modesty blur that appeared whenever the